# motoquencer, fader mode 2 in a linktonext chain: the gate-probability plate
# codes follow the FADER lane, including the linked `fadermode = 12` form (#84).
#
# motoquencer.md: "for accessing the parameters of the steps of the linked
# sequencer, add 10 to fadermode or buttonmode". So `fadermode = 12` means
# "chain member 1, mode 2 (gate probability)" -- the codes must come from THAT
# instance's own gateprob values, not the main's.
#
# The fader and the button/LED surfaces are addressed independently, and the
# plates belong to the BUTTON owner (buttoncolor-linked.gold). vcvoid therefore
# paints the gate-probability codes only on the instance that owns the faders in
# mode 2: an instance holding the plates while someone ELSE holds the faders
# keeps painting its buttonmode, which is the only thing it can honestly report
# about its own steps. The last block pins that case.
#
# Blink phases at tickrate 100 (half duty, free-running): 50% = 2 Hz, on for
# ticks 0..24 of each 50-tick cycle; 25% = 4 Hz, on for ticks 0..12 of each
# 25-tick cycle. No clock runs here, so there is no white played step anywhere.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock       = I1
    fadermode   = I2
    buttonmode  = I3
    numsteps    = 4
    numfaders   = 4
    defaultgate = 1
    linktonext  = 1
    cv          = O1
    gate        = O2
[motoquencer]
    defaultgate = 1
    cv          = O3
    gate        = O4
>>>
# fadermode 2 + buttonmode 0: the MAIN owns both surfaces. Its steps are all at
# the top notch, so every plate is steady blue.
@0 set I2 2
@0 set I3 0
@1 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@1 expect F1.color 1.2 tol 1e-6
@1 expect F2.color 1.2 tol 1e-6
# Dial the MAIN's step 2 down to notch 7 (idx 6, random 50%): it blinks at 2 Hz,
# so at tick 30 it is dark while the others stay lit.
@2 move F2 0.8571429
@30 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@30 expect F2.led 0 tol 1e-6
@30 expect F2.color 1.2 tol 1e-6
# fadermode 12 + buttonmode 10: the MEMBER owns both. Its own steps are all at
# notch 8, so tick 32 -- still inside the main's blink-off window -- shows four
# steady blue plates. The main's 50% step is not what these plates report.
@31 set I2 12
@31 set I3 10
@32 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@32 expect F1.color 1.2 tol 1e-6
@32 expect F2.led 1 tol 1e-6
@32 expect F2.color 1.2 tol 1e-6
# Dial the MEMBER's step 2 to notch 4 (idx 3, random 25%). Tick 63 is an off
# phase for 4 Hz but an ON phase for 2 Hz, so a dark lane 2 there is the
# member's own 25% rate and could not be the main's 50% one.
@33 move F2 0.4285714
@60 expect F2.led 1 tol 1e-6
@63 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@63 expect F2.led 0 tol 1e-6
@63 expect F2.color 1.2 tol 1e-6
# buttonmode back to 0 while fadermode stays 12: the MAIN owns the plates, the
# MEMBER owns the faders. The plate owner cannot speak for a lane it does not
# hold, so it paints its buttonmode-0 gate colour (0.1) and nothing blinks.
# Asserted one tick after the handover -- the outgoing owner releases the LEDs
# on the tick it loses them and the member ticks after the main
# (buttoncolor-linked.gold).
@64 set I3 0
@65 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@65 expect F1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@65 expect F2.led 1 tol 1e-6
@65 expect F2.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@88 expect F2.led 1 tol 1e-6
@88 expect F2.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
